Save a user prompt to persistent memory. Use this to record what the user asked — their intent, questions, and requests — so future sessions have context about the user's goals.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__engram__mem_save_prompt(args: {
  // The user's prompt text
  content: string;
  // Optional recovery target only after ambiguous_project. Ignored unless project_choice_reason is user_selected_after_ambiguous_project.
  project?: string;
  // Must be user_selected_after_ambiguous_project, and only after the user explicitly chose one of available_projects from an ambiguous_project error.
  project_choice_reason?: string;
  // Short-lived token returned by an ambiguous_project error. Required with project_choice_reason=user_selected_after_ambiguous_project.
  recovery_token?: string;
  // Session ID to associate with (default: manual-save-{project})
  session_id?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__engram__mem_search","description":"Engram provides persistent memory that survives across sessions and compactions.

