    project:"marketing-api",
    title:"Removed redundant GA4 Measurement Protocol path",
    type:"decision",
    scope:"project",
    topic_key:"architecture/dashboard-analytics-delivery",
    content:"**What**: Removed the synchronous GA4 Measurement Protocol request and unused `GA_API_SECRET`; Analytics now uses Firestore for durable server-side event storage and frontend gtag for GA4/Firebase Analytics.\\n**Why**: The dashboard has a valid Firebase web measurement ID but no Measurement Protocol API secret. Keeping both paths could block reruns and later duplicate events.\\n**Where**: dashboard/analytics.py; dashboard/config.py; .env.example\\n**Learned**: This intentionally accepts browser/ad-blocker loss for GA4 while Firestore retains the durable copy. Add Measurement Protocol back only if server-side GA4 delivery is explicitly required, with a secret and deduplication strategy."
